      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
          "content": "## Platform Observability Overview\nThis dashboard follows the current read-only platform boundary: Prometheus scrape health, backend API responsiveness, collector-backed snapshot signals, bounded persisted sync-history evidence, one bounded readiness-support posture slice, and a small amount of honest live-versus-persisted or backend-versus-collector comparison context where those metrics already exist.\n\nCurrent limits:\n- `app-api` and `gnmi-collector` expose meaningful metrics today.\n- Inventory, topology, policy, and bounded readiness-support freshness now surface where the backend already owns those metrics.\n- Collector read-path coverage, observation age, and detail-ready gaps are visualized here as numeric observability signals; the product-facing degraded-scope summaries still belong in `app-web`.\n- Collector-boundary latest fetch duration, configured timeout budget, and latest timeout or failure outcome are visualized here as observability-only signals; they explain fallback triggers but do not become product truth records or workflow meaning.\n- Cross-slice posture panels show freshness, persisted sync result mix, and current topology snapshot labels where those backend metrics already exist.\n- Topology partiality is now mirrored through three backend-owned cues where metrics expose them: inference posture, endpoint-pairing posture, and collection posture.\n- Readiness panels here show blocker, coverage, and persisted-snapshot posture only; they are not workflow verdicts or phase-transition control.\n- Comparison panels here show bounded aggregate deltas only; they are not drift engines or product truth.\n- Policy operational truth remains intentionally partial even though bounded policy sync evidence now exists.\n- ODL, Grafana, and Postgres exporter metrics remain future placeholders and are intentionally excluded from active panels.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "Dashboard Scope",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
